Wait, the standard Koszul formula for the Levi-Civita connection in coordinates:
`Γ^m_{ij} = ½ g^{mk} (∂_i g_{jk} + ∂_j g_{ik} - ∂_k g_{ij})`.
So with `g^{mk} = ginv m k`:
`Γ m i j x = ½ ∑ k, ginv m k x * (∂_i g_{j k} x + ∂_j g_{i k} x - ∂_k g_{i j} x)`.
